# Normalize line endings so the working tree is LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows checks out CRLF (core.autocrlf=true is its
# default), while `.prettierrc.json` pins `endOfLine: "lf"`. `npm run ci` then
# fails `format:check` on EVERY file — which is exactly how the v0.4.0 and
# v0.4.1 release builds died on the windows-latest runner: not a code problem,
# a checkout problem, reported as 130 style violations.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the repository (as it always did) and now also
# checks LF out, regardless of the developer's or the runner's autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.wasm binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
*.7z binary
*.gz binary
